    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (battalion "large number" multitude plurality)
  entry
    definition "a complete collection of similar things"
    id oewn-07973040-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "a convenient package or parcel (as of cigarettes or film)"
    id oewn-03876224-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "an association of criminals"
    examples ("police tried to break up the gang" "a pack of thieves")
    id oewn-08260983-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (gang ring mob)
  entry
    definition "an exclusive circle of people with a common purpose"
    id oewn-08257554-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (clique coterie ingroup "inner circle" camp)
  entry
    definition "a group of hunting animals"
    id oewn-08011383-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "a cream that cleanses and tones the skin"
    id oewn-03876658-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms ("face pack")
  entry
    definition "a sheet or blanket (either dry or wet) to wrap around the body for its therapeutic effect"
    id oewn-03876500-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "a bundle (especially one carried on the back)"
    id oewn-03876350-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "arrange in a container"
    examples ("pack the books into the boxes")
    id oewn-01485079-v
    partOfSpeech v
  entry
    definition "fill to capacity"
    examples ("This singer always packs the concert halls" "The murder trial packed the court house")
    id oewn-02091230-v
    partOfSpeech v
  entry
    definition "compress into a wad"
    examples ("wad paper into the box")
    id oewn-01486416-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (bundle wad compact)
  entry
    definition "carry, as on one's back"
    examples ("Pack your tents to the top of the mountain")
    id oewn-01453787-v
    partOfSpeech v
  entry
    definition "set up a committee or legislative body with one's own supporters so as to influence the outcome"
    examples ("pack a jury")
    id oewn-02401678-v
    partOfSpeech v
  entry
    definition "have with oneself; have on one's person"
    examples ("She always takes an umbrella" "I always carry money" "She packs a gun when she goes into the mountains")
    id oewn-02722977-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (carry take)
  entry
    definition "press tightly together or cram"
    examples ("The crowd packed the auditorium")
    id oewn-02068059-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (throng mob pile jam)
  entry
    definition "hike with a backpack"
    examples ("Every summer they are backpacking in the Rockies")
    id oewn-01929984-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (backpack)
  entry
    definition "press down tightly"
    examples ("tamp the coffee grinds in the container to make espresso")
    id oewn-01577402-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms ("tamp down" tamp)
  entry
    definition "seal with packing"
    examples ("pack the faucet")
    id oewn-01487510-v
    partOfSpeech v
  entry
    definition "have the property of being packable or of compacting easily"
    examples ("This powder compacts easily" "Such odd-shaped items do not pack well")
    id oewn-01486664-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (compact)
  entry
    definition "load with a pack"
    id oewn-01485761-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms ("load down")
  entry
    definition "treat the body or any part of it by wrapping it, as with blankets or sheets, and applying compresses to it, or stuffing it to provide cover, containment, or therapy, or to absorb blood"
    examples ("The nurse packed gauze in the wound" "You had better pack your swollen ankle with ice")
    id oewn-00108713-v
    partOfSpeech v
